<section xml:id="section-the-fundamental-theorems-of-calculus" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>
    The Fundamental Theorems of Calculus
  </title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      In this section, we develop the two <term> fundamental theorems of calculus </term>. These theorems bridge the two halves of calculus: differential calculus and integral calculus. We will see that differentiation and integration are related operations, and in a sense inverse to each other.
    </p>
  </introduction>

